WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.468
Doctor, how do you know if your patient actually took their medication?

2
00:00:04.918 --> 00:00:10.038
According to the WHO, adherence in chronic diseases is only around 50%.

3
00:00:11.338 --> 00:00:14.901
With several medications and schedules, it's easy to forget.

4
00:00:15.351 --> 00:00:20.684
Patients doubt whether they already took a dose, and in clinic, all you have is self-report.

5
00:00:21.134 --> 00:00:25.379
Sometimes a dose is increased, when the real problem was adherence.

6
00:00:26.679 --> 00:00:33.293
That's why we built MediTrack: reminders on the watch, confirmation with evidence, and an alert to the caregiver.

7
00:00:34.593 --> 00:00:39.158
It's 8:00. Rafael's watch vibrates: time for his metformin.

8
00:00:39.608 --> 00:00:43.661
As he takes it, the system gathers evidence: the hand-to-mouth gesture,

9
00:00:44.111 --> 00:00:48.677
the sequence of opening the bottle and drinking water, and his usual schedule.

10
00:00:49.127 --> 00:00:52.796
No single signal is proof; together, they build confidence.

11
00:00:53.246 --> 00:00:58.878
With strong evidence, the dose is confirmed automatically. If in doubt, the watch asks him.

12
00:01:08.593 --> 00:01:12.091
Elsewhere, his daughter Laura gets the confirmation on her phone.

13
00:01:12.541 --> 00:01:17.960
And if a dose has no evidence after 30 minutes, she gets an alert to give him a call.

14
00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:21.077
So caregivers don't have to keep watch all day.

15
00:01:30.593 --> 00:01:37.291
In clinic, you see every dose with its actual time, its delay, how it was confirmed, and with what confidence.

16
00:01:37.741 --> 00:01:42.435
And the patterns: for example, that the evening dose is the one most often missed.

17
00:01:42.885 --> 00:01:46.191
So you can adjust the regimen before increasing the dose.

18
00:01:47.491 --> 00:01:57.710
Wrist-based pill-taking detection has already been tested in a real-world study, DoseMate, with 94–95% balanced accuracy.

19
00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:05.435
Even so, "unconfirmed" doesn't mean "not taken", and MediTrack is not a medical device: it supports adherence.

20
00:02:06.735 --> 00:02:15.161
You can try the prototype online at christopherargenis.github.io/MediTrack. Or scan this code.

21
00:02:15.611 --> 00:02:19.963
We invite you to explore the app and see how MediTrack works. Thank you.
